<p>We first need to discuss how the game makes use of scripts, and in   particular our module event scripts (every mod has one). Every time   something happens in the game, e.g., you open or close the inventory,   talents, skills, or world map gui, all the module event scripts you  have  installed are fire and processed (probably in the order the mods  where  installed) as well as the core game scripts (typically these are   processed first). 
</p><p>So if we want to capture the behavior of our   NPC follower or a major event of the game it can be done here, e.g.,  the  PC selected or dropped the follower in the partypicker, you begin   travel, or the PC just finished talking to everyone at the gates in the   climax, or the game is over and we're at the slideshow.
</p><p>This  game  structure is indeed brilliant since it allows the main game and  all  mods installed to handle and process the same event, say <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/EVENT%20TYPE%20BEGIN%20TRAVEL" title="EVENT TYPE BEGIN TRAVEL">EVENT_TYPE_BEGIN_TRAVEL</a> or <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/EVENT%20TYPE%20MODULE%20HANDLE%20GIFT" title="EVENT TYPE MODULE HANDLE GIFT">EVENT_TYPE_MODULE_HANDLE_GIFT</a> or  <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/EVENT%20TYPE%20WORLD%20MAP%20CLOSED" title="EVENT TYPE WORLD MAP CLOSED">EVENT_TYPE_WORLD_MAP_CLOSED</a> and so forth.
</p>
